                        "entry_id": "06a81907-eab8-3719-b4fa-51edadea74b0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or relating to Henri-Louis Bergson (1859–1941), French philosopher, who convinced many thinkers that immediate experience and intuition are more significant than rationalism and science in understanding reality."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8eebb6c2-2925-41a5-bcf5-7b5748b342bf",
                                "sense_id": "78c663a2-4bfd-3b19-b788-317a27906ff5",
                                "text": "Jimmie, who was so lost in extensional ‘spatial’ time, was perfectly organised in Bergsonian ‘intentional’ time; what was fugitive, unsustainable, as formal structure, was perfectly stable, perfectly held, as art or will."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
